{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8oNiTCTRhVBuxFRjFi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. Nonrepresentational: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. The palette is restrained: deep indigo and charcoal ground, with a tense band of hot vermilion and ochre running diagonally from the lower left, cut through by a cool, pale grey-blue that hovers and resists. Brushwork alternates between fast, dragged gestural strokes that scrape and break, and slow, heavily loaded impasto passages with ridged, knife-made texture. Layering is dense in the center, where several translucent glazes build up and partly obscure one another, and thins toward the upper right into open, nearly bare ground with a few hesitant, unfinished marks. Rhythm comes from repeated short vertical flicks that pulse across the middle, interrupted by one long horizontal sweep that pulls against them. Spatial tension is created by a dark mass pressing in from the left edge against a field of lighter, looser color on the right. Leave deliberate pockets of empty space to let the composition breathe. The overall mood is urgent yet held back, precise in some areas and raw in others, with the surface visibly worked and uneven.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":16049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":461},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7845c8d4-5b8d-4a05-a63b-38eff7f8e028